    "created_at": "2019-03-11T08:53:08Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-03-11T08:53:08Z",
    "body": "The main thing I'm worried about is grabbing state from the object that should perhaps have been inaccessible to the caller. E.g., specifications cannot mutate the JavaScript object without bridging, and JavaScript cannot access private state without bridging.\r\n\r\nThis might also be more relevant when there's not necessarily a JavaScript side for an object and it's WebAssembly or some such? (Haven't thought too much about that though.)",
